          "deepDive": "**Nに至るまで** means *(all the way) to N, even N*. 至る means *to reach, to arrive at*, so the phrase marks the **far end of a range** and stresses that **everything** within it is included. It very often pairs with から: **AからBに至るまで** *from A all the way to B*.\n\nTwo uses (both in the book's explanation):\n- **A range** of places or times: 関東地方から東北地方に至るまで, 明治時代から現在に至るまで.\n- **An extreme endpoint** that shows how wide the range is — something very small and detailed or very large: 髪の毛1本に至るまで, 電源プラグから宇宙開発用ロボットに至るまで. The implication is *even that is included, so of course everything in between is too*.\n\nThe second half therefore talks about the whole range: すべて, 全て, さまざまな, あらゆる, 広範囲に及ぶ. In the sample text: 大人はもとより小さな子どもに至るまで、あらゆる人々が楽しめる. It is formal and written (the book's icon: not used when chatting with friends or family).\n\nCompare:\n- **〜まで**: plain *until / as far as*, with no emphasis on how wide the range is.\n- **〜にかけて** (*from … through …*): a loose span of time or space (東北地方から関東北部にかけて広い範囲で積雪) — neutral, no sense of *even*.\n- **〜にわたって** (*throughout, over*): a whole period or area (3年間にわたって放送された). ✗3年間に至るまで.\n\nThe clip note covers the verb **に至る** *to reach (a stage or state)*: 作るに至った経緯 *how she came to make…*. Related forms: **〜に至っては** *as for ~ (an extreme case)* (point #7) and the idiom **事ここに至っては** *now that things have come to this*. The review questions use に至って, に至っても, に至っては and に至った as options.\n\nJLPT tip: when the options include に至るまで, にかけて and にわたって, look at the second half: an emphatic すべて／あらゆる／さまざまな points to に至るまで; a simple span of area points to にかけて; a period + continuing action points to にわたって.",
